    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-46ml-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the National Children’s Commissioner has reason to believe that a Commonwealth government agency has information or a document relevant to the performance by the Commissioner of functions under this Part, the Commissioner may give a written notice to the agency requiring the agency:  (a) to give the information to the Commissioner in writing signed by or on behalf of the agency; or  (b) to produce the document to the Commissioner." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the National Children’s Commissioner has reason to believe that a Commonwealth government agency has information or a document relevant to the performance by the Commissioner of functions under this Part, the Commissioner may give a written notice to the agency requiring the agency:  (a) to give the information to the Commissioner in writing signed by or on behalf of the agency; or  (b) to produce the document to the Commissioner."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "23d4d3e65ae04b9deec17cbe3658f09f25d1ce6f1e1b05ef0ee6e42c1ed0862d" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-human-rights-commission-amendment-national-children-s-commissioner-act-2012-sch-1-sec-46ml ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Agency must provide information or document to the Commissioner upon request." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
